<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Viceroyalty of Carchemish</h1><p class="st-meta">1340 BCE – 1180 BCE (approx.) · capital Carchemish</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Hittite viceroyalty of Carchemish, which governed Syria for the Hittite kings and outlived the empire's fall.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-carchemish">Carchemish</a>, a great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> crossing city, after a siege c. 1327 BCE, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire's</a> hold on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a>. He made his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharri-kushuh">Piyassili</a>, known by the Hurrian name Sharri-Kushuh, king of Carchemish.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-carchemish">Carchemish</a> acted as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroys</a> for the Hittite great king, supervising Syrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-ugarit">Ugarit</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emar">Emar</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-amurru">Amurru</a>, settling their disputes and collecting tribute. They belonged to the Hittite royal family and kept a court with Hurrian and Luwian traditions.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> fell around 1180 BCE, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-carchemish">Carchemish</a> survived. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuzi-teshub">Kuzi-Teshub</a> took the title great king, and his heirs founded the Neo-Hittite Kingdom of Carchemish and kingdoms such as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/melid">Melid</a>, carrying Hittite traditions into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1340 BCE – 1180 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:33.03%;width:3.18%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1340 BCE – 1180 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century-bce">14th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Carchemish</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Piyassili, Ini-Teshub, Talmi-Teshub</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hittite and Hurrian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hittite, Luwian, Akkadian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hittite Carchemish</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1260&amp;focus=viceroyalty-of-carchemish" aria-label="Viceroyalty of Carchemish on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5634 850 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Viceroyalty of Carchemish lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5954 1106L5961 1135M5954 1106L5904 1147M5954 1106L5852 1002M5954 1106L5954 1106M5954 1106L5954 1055"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5961 1135h0M5904 1147h0M5852 1002h0M5954 1106h0M5954 1055h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5954 1106h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5954 1106h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Carchemish. <a href="/atlas?year=-1260&amp;focus=viceroyalty-of-carchemish">On the atlas &rarr